From: distsystem <dev@dist.systems>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu/vpe: keep DPM0 idle-gate on Strix Halo PMFW 100.6.0

Upstream 3ac635367eb5 ("drm/amd: Check that VPE has reached DPM0 in idle
handler") reschedules VPE power-down until VPE has reached DPM0, so
PowerDownVpe never fires into a busy SMU after resume. But it gates that
behaviour behind vpe_need_dpm0_at_power_down(): for VPE IP 6.1.1 it only
applies when pm.fw_version < 0x0a640500.

The ASUS ProArt PX13 (Strix Halo) reports VPE IP 6.1.1 and SMU PMFW
100.6.0 (pm.fw_version 0x0a640600) - one step above that gate - yet still
soft-locks for tens of seconds after resume on the same PowerDownVpe ->
"SMU: No response msg_reg: 32" path. The PMFW assumption that >=
0x0a640500 is fixed does not hold here, so the upstream fix is compiled
in but never engages on PX13.

Force the DPM0 wait for VPE 6.1.1 regardless of PMFW version. The check
is a no-op once VPE is already at DPM0, so it only adds the reschedule
when actually needed. Replaces our earlier 0019 (raise VPE_IDLE_TIMEOUT
to 2s); the condition-based DPM0 wait is the upstream-preferred mechanism.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vpe.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vpe.c
@@ -326,7 +326,14 @@
 {
 	switch (amdgpu_ip_version(adev, VPE_HWIP, 0)) {
 	case IP_VERSION(6, 1, 1):
-		return adev->pm.fw_version < 0x0a640500;
+		/*
+		 * PX13 (Strix Halo) ships SMU PMFW 100.6.0 (pm.fw_version
+		 * 0x0a640600), >= upstream's 0x0a640500 gate, yet still wedges
+		 * the SMU on PowerDownVpe after resume - the firmware check
+		 * wrongly assumes >= 0x0a640500 is fixed. Force the DPM0 wait
+		 * on this VPE regardless of PMFW version.
+		 */
+		return true;
 	default:
 		return false;
 	}
